WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.830
In 1352, a Moroccan legal scholar named
Ibn Battuta crossed the Sahara to the

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.420
kingdom of Mali.

3
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.950
He found crowds at Friday prayer, and
people working hard to learn the Qur'an

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.090
by heart.

5
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:18.160
Thousands of miles from Mecca, Islam
was already well established there.

6
00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:25.040
So between 1200 and 1450, who actually
carried religions across oceans and deserts?

7
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.480
In this mission, you'll trace
the great routes of the time:

8
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:32.110
the Silk Roads, the Indian
Ocean and the Sahara.

9
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.900
Then you'll visit Angkor Wat, a temple
built for Vishnu that later became a place

10
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.440
of Buddhist worship.

11
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:43.460
Your mission: find out who really carried
religions across oceans and deserts,

12
00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.200
and how.
